So I've been playing Samurai and Cavemen lately. It brings to mind a
couple questions regarding projectiles, in bullet point form:

--Do launchers such as slings or bows gain skill experience when you
bash monsters with them, or only via firing the proper projectiles? I
thought it clever to ditch the Caveman's club, but it seems that
bashing with the sling does very little to get me to expert any
quicker.
--Flint stones from a sling do double the damage of ordinary rocks,
but are difficult to find. Is there even any way to get them in
quantities apart from wishing?
--And for my last question, shurikens and boomerangs. They're very
nice, but given how hard it is to get them in any quantity, as well as
their propensity to break when thrown, is training either to skill to
expert even a feasible proposition?


